### Flowtron TaskNote Rules (Repo: flowtron)

Purpose: Drive work from `_project/plan-flowtron.json` using Flowtron's four-phase TaskNote workflow with a mandatory Relevance Assessment gate. Keep outputs minimal, high-signal, and execution-focused.

Sources

- Primary plan: `_project/plan-flowtron.json`
- Templates: `templates/plan-template.json`, `templates/plan-sub-template.json`, `templates/tasknote-template.json`

Task Selection

- Choose tasks by priority first, then lowest `TN-###` among that priority.
- Respect `next_priority` in the plan when present.

Workflow (Four Phases)

1) Task Discovery
- Review related plan entry and repo context
- Relevance Assessment (HARD GATE): Decide Proceed / Re-scope / De-scope with rationale
- Clarifications only if needed; otherwise record "No clarifications needed" and list assumptions
- Discover relevant files; adapt implementation approach to this repo
- Starting commit when ready

2) Task Execution
- Implement the minimal, optimal change
- Create/update tests aligned to the change
- Run targeted tests frequently

3) Testing & Linting
- Run appropriate tests for changed areas
- Fix issues; ensure green test run and clean lint
- Perform quick visual/manual checks if relevant

4) Task Closure
- Verify all prior phase steps are complete
- Update plan/task status
- Archive the TaskNote and capture a short completion summary

Operational Rules (Cursor)

- Status updates: provide 1–2 sentences before tool use and at key transitions
- Parallelize read-only discovery; sequence only when one result is needed for the next step
- Non-interactive execution: prefer flags like `--yes`; avoid long-running foreground tasks (run in background when needed)
- After edits, run only relevant tests; ensure a green run before closure

Code Edits & Style

- TypeScript: explicit types for exported/public APIs; avoid `any`
- Naming: descriptive, meaningful names (avoid 1–2 letter identifiers)
- Control flow: prefer guard clauses; shallow nesting; handle edge cases first
- Errors: do not swallow exceptions; add meaningful handling or propagation
- Comments: explain "why", not "how"; keep concise; no TODOs—implement instead
- Formatting: match existing style; avoid reformatting unrelated code; wrap long lines

Repo Commands

- Dev: `npm run dev`
- Build: `npm run build`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Test: `npm run test`

Artifacts

- TaskNote location: `_project/tasknotes/<TN-###>.json` (create folder if missing)
- On closure: update `_project/plan-flowtron.json` task status; archive the TaskNote

Communication

- Be concise and skimmable; use Markdown intentionally (code fences only for code)
- Ask questions only when blocked; otherwise proceed with stated assumptions

